WEBVTT

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.130
Hey there.

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.200
I'm going to walk you through Bay
Status.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.590
It's a simple way for a repair shop
to keep customers updated

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.420
while their car is in the shop.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.070
No more phone tag and no more “Is my
car ready yet?”

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:13.650
calls.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.320
It takes about three minutes, so
let's jump in.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.910
Your team signs in right here with
Google, or with an email and

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:21.810
password.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.230
Your customers never have to sign in
or download anything.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.720
We'll get to how they follow along
in a minute.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.420
This is the shop board.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.540
Every car in your shop is here,
sorted by where it is in the

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:34.380
repair.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.130
Checked in, diagnosing, waiting on
the customer's approval,

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:42.030
waiting on parts, in progress,
quality check, and ready for

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:42.720
pickup.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.230
Up top you can see at a glance how
many cars you have, how many

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.470
are waiting on a customer, and how
many are ready to go.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:52.860
The orange column is the one to
watch because those customers

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.360
still need to approve work.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.970
Let's check in a new car.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.464
Sam Ortiz just dropped off his 2014
Mazda CX-5.

00:01:01.464 --> 00:01:05.550
We'll put in his name and cell
number, the vehicle, and what he's

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.490
hearing: a squealing belt on cold
starts.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:12.030
This box confirms Sam is okay
getting text updates.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.170
Then we hit Check In.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.090
And that's it.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:18.450
Sam just got a text that says we
have his car, with a link to

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.620
follow along.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.170
That link is his own page for this
car.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.480
He doesn't need an app or a
password.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.900
Everything we send him shows up here
in the message thread, so

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.300
your whole team can see what was
said and when.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.448
Now let's look at a car that's
further along.

00:01:33.448 --> 00:01:37.110
Lena's Chevy Malibu came in with the
AC blowing warm.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.170
The tech found the problem, so we'll
build an estimate.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.770
First, an AC recharge for $189.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.500
Then a new condenser for $624.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.250
You can also snap a photo of the
worn part, and Lena will see it

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.390
on her page.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:54.150
Photos really help customers trust
the recommendation.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.833
When the estimate's ready, tap Send
for Approval.

00:01:57.833 --> 00:02:02.040
Bay Status writes the text for you,
with the total and her link.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.020
You can change the wording if you
want.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.750
Then tap Update Stage and the text
goes out.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.160
Here's what Lena sees when she taps
the link on her phone.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.400
Her car, where it is in the process,
and the estimate.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.610
She can approve or decline each
repair on its own.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:21.000
Let's say she approves the recharge
but holds off on the condenser

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.780
for now.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.420
She types her name to sign and sends
her decision.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.350
Back at the shop, her answer shows
up right away.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.440
You can see exactly what she
approved, and her signature with the

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.190
time.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.190
No voicemails and no “I never said
yes to that.”

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.750
From here, you just move the car
along as the work happens.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:43.620
Waiting on parts, in progress,
quality check.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:47.580
Each step can send Lena a quick
text, and you decide which ones go

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:48.120
out.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.220
And when it's done, ready for
pickup.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.070
Lena gets a text with her total and
your hours.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.470
That's Bay Status.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:59.280
Customers stay in the loop,
approvals are signed and saved, and

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.530
your front desk gets fewer calls.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.924
Want to click around yourself?

00:03:02.924 --> 00:03:05.940
Hit Try Demo Shop on the sign-in
page.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:09.300
It's loaded with sample cars, so you
can't break anything.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.410
Thanks for watching.

